<title>ITALY: Details of Italian April new car registrations.</title>
<headline>Details of Italian April new car registrations.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a table of Italian new car registrations for April, released by the Italian Transport Ministry.</p>
<p>Earlier the Ministry said Italian new car registrations rose 52.37 percent to 231,500 units in April, compared with 151,933 in April 1996.</p>
<p>	     Apr 97 registrations Mkt shre    Apr 96  Mkt shre</p>
<p>Fiat			 103,950   44.90	 67,389  44.35</p>
<p>Volkswagen		  23,550   10.30	 18,183  11.93</p>
<p>Ford			  21,440    9.26	 14,977   9.86</p>
<p>General Motors	    18,970    8.19	 12,191   8.13</p>
<p>PSA Peugeot		 16,720    7.22	  8,906   5.86</p>
<p>Renault		     16,630    7.18	  9,641   6.35</p>
<p>BMW			    8,790    3.80	  6,578   4.33</p>
<p>Mercedes		     3,540    1.53	  2,887   1.90</p>
<p>Nissan			 4,260    1.84	  2,758   1.82</p>
<p>Volvo			  2,600    1.12	  1,771   1.17</p>
<p>NOTE - Fiat comprises Fiat, Alfa Romeo, Lancia Autobianchi, and Fiat-Innocenti. Volkswagen comprises VW, Audi, Skoda and Seat. General Motors comprises Opel and Saab. PSA-Peugeot comprises Peugeot and Citroen. BMW comprises BMW and Rover.</p>
<p>-- Milan bureau +392 66129502</p>
